        "title": "Lorenz ratio in a chain of Coulomb islands",
        "claim": "In the Heat Coulomb Blockade regime, the normalized Lorenz ratio L/L0 depends on the chain length M and the number of chiral channels N. For N=1, L/L0 is exactly 1; for N=2, L/L0 grows approximately as sqrt(M+1)/2 in the large chain limit.",
        "source": {
          "citation": "Patrice Roche, Breakdown of the Wiedemann-Franz Law in an Interacting Quantum Hall Metamaterial, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/twbt-z82z",
